cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SecHelix in academic work, tooling, or a security program, please cite it as below."
title: SecHelix
abstract: >-
  An evidence-first application-security Agent Skill for authorized
  repositories and environments. SecHelix maps attack surfaces, selects
  applicable security hypotheses from a structured catalog of security
  families and verification lenses, independently verifies material
  findings, fixes root causes, requires regression proof, and produces
  explicit release decisions. Every catalog record is an unverified
  hypothesis until an evidence chain supports it; High and Critical
  severity claims require independent verification.
type: software
